data.content:
Here are the four breaking changes and their fixes:

---

### 1. `GenericShift.cs` — Consistent shift behavior in generic math

In .NET 9, shift operations on small types (`byte`, `short`, etc.) via `IShiftOperators<T,int,T>` were **inconsistent** — `ShiftLeft<byte>(0xFF, 8)` returned `0`. In .NET 10, shift behavior is now **consistent** across all types, meaning results may differ from .NET 9. If your code relied on the old overflow/truncation behavior, add explicit masking:

```csharp
static T ShiftLeft<T>(T value, int amount) where T : IShiftOperators<T, int, T>
    => value << amount;
// Review all callers — results for byte/short/ushort may now differ.
// Add explicit casts or masks if you depended on the old behavior.
```

### 2. `ApiClient.cs` — Streaming HTTP responses enabled by default in Blazor WASM

In .NET 10, **streaming responses are enabled by default** in browser-based HTTP clients. The `stream.Read(...)` synchronous call will fail because the stream is now a non-seekable streaming response. Fix by using **async reads**:

```csharp
var response = await httpClient.GetAsync(url);
var stream = await response.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
var buffer = new byte[4096];
int bytesRead = await stream.ReadAsync(buffer, 0, buffer.Length); // async
```

### 3. `Archiver.cs` — PaxTarEntry no longer includes atime/ctime by default

In .NET 10, `PaxTarEntry` **no longer auto-populates `AccessTime` and `ChangeTime`**. If you need them, set them explicitly:

```csharp
var entry = new PaxTarEntry(TarEntryType.RegularFile, "data.txt");
var now = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;
entry.AccessTime = now;
entry.ChangeTime = now;
archive.WriteEntry(entry);
```

### 4. `App.csproj` + HTTP/3 — HTTP/3 stripped when trimming

With `<PublishTrimmed>true</PublishTrimmed>`, **HTTP/3 code is entirely removed by the trimmer** in .NET 10. Your backend connections over HTTP/3 will silently downgrade or fail. Fix by adding:

```xml
<PropertyGroup>
  <PublishTrimmed>true</PublishTrimmed>
  <Http3Support>true</Http3Support>
</PropertyGroup>
```
